Our analysis produces an odds ratio (OR) that informs whether tRNA charging and modification or any pair of modifications tend to appear together in the same read (OR > 1, stimulatory crosstalk) or tend to be exclusive of one another (OR < 1, inhibitory crosstalk), as well as calculates the significance of this interdependence using Fisher's exact test. Given that the tRNA-seq data in general has very high coverage for each tRNA species, hundreds to thousands of pairs for a specific tRNA can be analyzed simultaneously and the resulting p-values are FDR-corrected for multiple comparisons. We implemented our method within the open-source mim-tRNA-seq computational pipeline (
10
) (
https://github.com/nedialkova-lab/mim-tRNAseq
).
